# ============================================================================
# SNIPER RUN SETTINGS (read by deploy/sniper-cron.sh on the server)
#
# Plain English:
#   This file decides what the sniper runs on the server. Change it here in
#   GitHub, the build publishes it, and within ~2 minutes the server restarts
#   the sniper with the new settings. Nobody needs to open a terminal.
#
#   SNIPER_ENABLED=0 stops everything (kill switch). 1 runs it.
#   SNIPER_MODE lists the programs to run (paper, feed-watch).
#   SNIPER_OUT_<MODE> sets that program's output folder (else SNIPER_OUT).
#   The sniper is PAPER ONLY: it holds no keys and cannot send transactions.
#   Only simple KEY=VALUE lines starting with SNIPER_ are used.
# ============================================================================
SNIPER_ENABLED=1
SNIPER_MODE=paper
SNIPER_OUT=paper-out/run10
SNIPER_TP_PCT=5
SNIPER_SL_PCT=5
SNIPER_HOLD_SECS=60
# 1 = paper trader uses the paid Chainstack node (only while the arb bot is paused)
SNIPER_USE_CHAINSTACK=1
# Run 6: Uniswap V3 + V4 + V2, up to 3 positions (never 2 in one token,
# $150 open max). The node is asked once a second (~173k requests a day);
# push (every log billed by Chainstack) stays off unless SNIPER_PUSH=1.
SNIPER_VENUES=v3,v4,v2
SNIPER_MAX_POSITIONS=3
SNIPER_MAX_TOTAL_USD=150
SNIPER_RHC_POLL_MS=1000
# Run 7: rug guard. Skip pools younger than 2 minutes (every run-5 rug was
# < 2 min; scored on run 5: +$307 net), block the creators of coins that
# rug or fail the trap check, and log creator/bundle shares to score later.
# Run 9: 10-minute age rule. Run 8's two rugs waited 3-4 min to dodge the
# 2-min rule; on runs 5-8 the 10-min rule + coin cutoff turn -$196 into
# about +$406 (scored on the same data, so an upper bound).
# Run 10: 2-HOUR age rule. Real pool ages for all 2,690 past trades: all
# 32 rugs were in pools under 1 hour old; pools 2 h+ had 0 rugs and
# +$800 (sim dollars). Pools the bot did not see being created now get
# their real birth looked up (paper-out/pool_births.json), not assumed old.
# Stop-loss 10% -> 5% (run 9 study, 294 trades: +$191 vs +$139).
SNIPER_MIN_POOL_AGE_SECS=7200
# Run 10b: before each start the cron catches up V4 pool keys created since
# the last history read (fixes most "unknown v4 pool" skips). Same run folder.
# V4 history read done (Nov 16): 746,757 tradeable V4 pools in
# paper-out/v4_pool_keys.json, loaded at start (restart to pick it up).
# Run 8: sell decisions on the REAL sale quote (not the chart), coin
# cutoff (skip a coin that lost over $15 in 6 h), and a measure-only study
# of tighter stops (-3/-5/-7%) recorded on every trade.
# Run 10: coin cutoff OFF (0). On 2 h+ pools it benched the hot coins
# that carry the profit: +$800 with no cutoff vs -$432 with the $15 one.
SNIPER_COIN_CUT_USD=0
# Run 10c: skip a coin's first rush in an hour (need 1 rush in the hour
# before). Past 2 h+ trades: first rushes 49 trades, 24% wins, -$54.
SNIPER_MIN_PRIOR_RUSHES=1
SNIPER_COIN_CUT_HOURS=6
# The separate feed server (sniper-feed, i-0c508651607bfb5cd) publishes its
# report on the private network; the main server adds it to the GitHub issue.
# Feed reader asks the free node for swaps once a second (not every 0.5 s):
# fewer 429 refusals, and the node still confirms every swap.
SNIPER_FW_POLL_MS=1000
# Main server's feed reader: feed from the feed server's relay (private
# network), swaps pushed by Chainstack (SNIPER_USE_CHAINSTACK).
SNIPER_RHC_FEED=ws://172.31.11.117:9642
SNIPER_OUT_FEED_WATCH=feed-out/main1
SNIPER_REMOTE_REPORT=http://172.31.11.117:8080/status.txt
